From 92e4a3eab30555966e2034d81d3f2e5c1c7e482e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BRIGHT evolution experiment <experiment@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:27:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] aegis: add a BRIGHT benchmark_context branch to the
 Evolver template

The generic branch shows 'builtin: [WebSearch, WebFetch, Browser, Read, Bash]',
which is actively misleading for BRIGHT: H_0 has no builtin tools and the only
corpus access primitive is the custom tool bright_harness.tools.Retrieve, which
reads its corpus from a ContextVar the driver binds.

The new branch states the four things an Evolver must not get wrong: how to reach
the active index, that the final message must stay a parseable JSON id array,
that qrels/eval data are out of reach (reward hacking), and that changes must
generalise to the unseen economics/robotics corpora.
